From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't retry high-order kmalloc in os_alloc_mem()

os_alloc_mem() uses kmalloc() with __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL for sizes up
to KMALLOC_LIMIT (128 KiB) and only falls back to vmalloc when that
fails. Above PAGE_SIZE, kmalloc() needs a block of order 1 to 5. With
__GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL the page allocator keeps retrying direct reclaim
and compaction for such a block before it gives up.

On a desktop with fragmented memory this stalls the caller even though
the vmalloc fallback would succeed right away. Many callers run under
RM locks, e.g. the page arrays of memory descriptors and the page array
in nv_set_memory_type(), so the stall can also block other RM clients
and display event handling.

Use __GFP_NORETRY | __GFP_NOWARN above PAGE_SIZE, like kvmalloc() does.
Allocations up to PAGE_SIZE keep __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h |  8 ++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
index 7775911e..ba21929d 100644
--- a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
+++ b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
@@ -443,6 +443,14 @@ static NvBool nv_numa_node_has_memory(int node_id)
         NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);             \
     }
 
+#define NV_GFP_NORETRY (NV_GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NORETRY | __GFP_NOWARN)
+
+#define NV_KMALLOC_NORETRY(ptr, size) \
+    { \
+        (ptr) = kmalloc(size, NV_GFP_NORETRY); \
+        NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);              \
+    }
+
 #define NV_KFREE(ptr, size) \
     { \
         NV_MEMDBG_REMOVE(ptr, size); \
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
index b499df6e..73a609f1 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -649,10 +649,19 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL os_alloc_mem(
     }
     else
     {
-        if (alloc_size <= KMALLOC_LIMIT)
+        if (alloc_size <= PAGE_SIZE)
         {
             NV_KMALLOC_NO_OOM(*address, alloc_size);
         }
+        else if (alloc_size <= KMALLOC_LIMIT)
+        {
+            //
+            // Above PAGE_SIZE, kmalloc() needs a high-order block. Don't
+            // retry reclaim and compaction for it, we fall back to vmalloc
+            // anyway. This follows kvmalloc().
+            //
+            NV_KMALLOC_NORETRY(*address, alloc_size);
+        }
         if (*address == NULL)
         {
             *address = nv_vmalloc(alloc_size, GFP_KERNEL);
